{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Daniel Mercer jolted awake to the harsh, pixelated glow of sunlight casting jagged shadows across his bedroom floor. He rubbed his eyes, expecting another hangover-fueled headache, but the pain in his skull felt different—not throbbing, but *tingling*, like static electricity buzzing under his skin. He glanced at his hands; the veins were sharp, geometric lines, and his fingers moved with an unnatural, stuttering precision when he flexed them. The digital clock on his nightstand read **06:00 AM**, but the numbers flickered like a corrupted file, glitching between times he didn’t recognize. His breath hitched as he realized the coffee mug on his desk—once chipped and well-loved—was now pristine, its surface reflecting the warped textures of his own skin. He stood, his socks sticking faintly to the floor like a cheap simulation’s physics, and stepped into the hallway. The sound of his footsteps wasn’t organic; it was a synthetic *thud*, the audio looping just slightly out of sync with his movement.\n\nThe living room was wrong. The couch, once sagging from years of use, now had a perfect, unblemished stitching pattern, and the throw pillow’s embroidered initials pulsed with a faint, neon-blue glow. Daniel’s blood turned to ice as he spotted his gaming console on the shelf—*his* console, an old model he’d bought in high school—now displaying a message in bold, blocky font: **\"SYSTEM OVERLOAD DETECTED. PLAYER AWARENESS: 12%.\"** He lunged for it, slamming his palm against the screen, but it didn’t react; his touch passed through the glass like a ghost’s. A high-pitched, mechanical voice echoed through the room, not from the console but from *everywhere*: **\"WELCOME TO LEVEL 1, PLAYER. OBJECTIVES WILL BE ASSIGNED UPON COMPLETION OF INITIAL SEQUENCE.\"** Daniel’s stomach lurched as he noticed the floorboards beneath his feet had transformed—now a grid of glowing coordinates, like a map. Outside his window, the sky wasn’t just blue; it was a gradient of colors shifting in real-time, as if the game’s rendering engine was fighting to keep up with his panic. He backed away slowly, his mind racing, until his heel struck something solid. He looked down. A controller had appeared on the floor, brand-new, its buttons labeled **\"JUMP,\" \"ATTACK,\"** and **\"CONFIRM.\"** The screen on the back flickered with a single word: **\"PLAY?\"**", "logprobs": [{"token": "Daniel", "logprob": -1.6121129989624023}, {"token": " Mercer", "logprob": -0.27265679836273193}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -1.1157020330429077}, {"token": "olt", "logprob": -0.0011179156135767698}, {"token": "ed", "logprob": -1.8358061424805783e-05}, {"token": " awake", "logprob": -0.012841272167861462}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.36262747645378113}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.07688237726688385}, {"token": " harsh", "logprob": -2.251866102218628}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.5070276260375977}, {"token": " pixel", "logprob": -1.1115622520446777}, {"token": "ated", "logprob": -0.00014804698002990335}, {"token": " glow", "logprob": -0.6764836311340332}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.020440174266695976}, {"token": " sunlight", "logprob": -1.7138481140136719}, {"token": " casting", "logprob": -3.7767224311828613}, {"token": " jag", "logprob": -0.23922383785247803}, {"token": "ged", "logprob": -1.0013530300057027e-05}, {"token": " shadows", "logprob": -0.2598382830619812}, {"token": " across", "logprob": -0.029176075011491776}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.19204968214035034}, {"token": " bedroom", "logprob": -0.38679951429367065}, {"token": " floor", "logprob": -1.363342523574829}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.0320880189538002}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.7114851474761963}, {"token": " rubbed", "logprob": -0.6223356127738953}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.006302007474005222}, {"token": " eyes", "logprob": -0.34573230147361755}, {"token": "